# BusGo conventions

TypeScript strict mode stays on. Do not use `any`, `@ts-ignore`, or `as` to skip a real type.

Use function components. Do not use class components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
class SearchPage extends React.Component {}

// ✅ GOOD
export function SearchPage() {
  return <main>Search buses</main>;
}
```

Style with Tailwind utility classes only. Do not add CSS modules, styled-components, or new component stylesheets.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button style={{ backgroundColor: "#d84e55" }}>Search</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="rounded-2xl bg-brand px-6 font-extrabold text-white">Search</button>
```

HTTP handlers live under `app/api` as `route.ts` files. Do not add a `pages/api` route.

Validate request bodies and search params with Zod before use.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const seatIds = body.seatIds as string[];

// ✅ GOOD
const payload = bookingSchema.parse(body);
```

Read and write the database only through `lib/db.ts`. Do not construct a Prisma or Postgres client inside a route, page, or component.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
import { Pool } from "pg";
const pool = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL });

// ✅ GOOD
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
```
